Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 05:40:29 +0200
Subject: [parser] Preserve first strict parameter and arrow declaration error

Previously, `ParserFormalParameters::set_strict_parameter_error`,
`ExpressionScope::RecordStrictModeParameterError`, and
`ArrowHeadParsingScope::RecordDeclarationError` unconditionally
overwrote any previously recorded error location and message.

As a result, eager functions and arrow functions with multiple strict
parameter errors (such as `(function(implements, eval) { "use strict"; })`
or `(implements, eval) => { "use strict"; }`) or multiple arrow
parameter declaration errors (such as `([a.b], 1) => {}`) reported the
last error in the parameter list instead of the first, and disagreed
with lazy function parsing.

Keep the first recorded error when one is already valid.

Bug: 567222737
